Read graphs, interpolate, and question a visual claim (@ql-graphs: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @quantitative-literacy, #source @ql-source-prealgebra, #source @ql-source-algebra, #quantitative-literacy "Exponential-and-logarithmic-scales.lingua#r_0NQPY7MA3SJ3TR97ZJRTW7ZQPG", #geology "../../../../gaia/earth/geology/field/Read-a-topographic-and-geological-map.lingua#r_7W0VVA0MX0Z4K810G34SAMHSZC", #clean-manufacturing "../../../production/clean-manufacturing-and-contamination-control/foundations/A-distribution-is-more-than-an-average-size.lingua#r_1AXAAEZSZECHDWQ0GVPERT8S5Z") { r_2GDCZSQKNW5BCGN7B5D9G36HK2
**Read:** Prealgebra 2e chapter 11 for coordinates and lines; Algebra and Trigonometry 2e sections on rates of change, behavior of graphs, and fitting linear models. Inspect actual axes and tabulated examples rather than reading only the captions.

Name each axis, its unit, scale, origin, and population or time interval. The slope Δy/Δx has units. An area under a rate-versus-time graph has the unit of an accumulated quantity; summing unweighted heights on unequal time intervals generally does not estimate that area correctly.

Linear interpolation between (x₀,y₀) and (x₁,y₁) gives y = y₀ + (y₁ − y₀)(x − x₀)/(x₁ − x₀). It assumes a straight segment for this purpose. Interpolating across a phase change or an abrupt switching event may be unjustified. A smooth rendered curve does not prove smooth physical behavior.

For a flow of 10 L/min for 2 min and 4 L/min for 5 min, the total is 40 L and the time-weighted average is 40/7 L/min. The unweighted mean of the two flow readings, 7 L/min, answers a different question. A graph truncated at a convenient vertical origin can also exaggerate a relative visual change.

**Work:** draw the flow example as a step plot and recover its total by rectangles. Read a point from a published technical graph and report the uncertainty introduced by image resolution separately from the underlying experiment's uncertainty. Present the same data with linear and logarithmic axes and explain which comparisons each display supports. Never silently replace absent observations with zero.

